  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visit Circular Economy Innovation Exchange (CERF25NG2O)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity involved the organisation of the study visit &quot;Circular Economy Innovation Exchange&quot; hosted by CERF, the Netherlands consulate-general in Lagos, the Circular Business Platform in Lagos and Holland Circular Hotspot.The programme brought five Nigerian stakeholders from the public and private sectors to the Netherlands to exchange knowledge on circular economy solutions in waste management and the bioeconomy.The visit facilitated meetings with Dutch companies and institutions and helped explore potential partnerships, including collaborations on materials recovery facilities, refuse derived fuel and the valorisation of mango waste streams. It also strengthened engagement with Nigerian state authorities and financial partners.As a follow-up, Invest International initiated a webinar with several Nigerian states to present investment opportunities in waste recovery, recycling and the bioeconomy.</narrative>
  </description>
